\caption(Both clouds use the same side count, but their rotations differ. The left panel shows positive support-dot counts on log2 axes; the right retains every actual query count. Each printed count satisfies dots=2n×queries and comparisons=dots−support calls.)
\alttext(Two panels display actual scanned vertices and Minkowski query counts for ten regular polygon sizes from three to one thousand twenty-four. Counts include initialization and all stored vertices. Every distance, loop visit and comparison count is printed.)

> Separate record quotas, loop budgets and generated vertices

`gjk_distance_trace()` retains actual fixed-size state records online. The quota
counts complete records, including initial and stopping metadata; it does not
count numeric entries, bytes or peak RAM. The inputs, root object, ordinary result
and final feature, constant working storage and allocator overhead are excluded.
No numerical replay, truncation or partial trace is returned. Zero disables only
the optional record quota. A separated singleton pair needs four records, while
a near-origin pair needs three and an empty input one. Because zero means quota
off, it is not a way to reject the one-record empty history.

The iteration budget counts loop visits, with zero meaning initialize and return
the initial approximation with `iteration_limit`. The polygon generator instead
checks its whole output vertex count before allocation. These are different units.
Complete finite-coordinate validation precedes empty, loop-budget and history
handling; a late invalid point cannot be hidden behind a cheap early exit.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/gjk_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/gjk.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

 const std::vector<dm::geometry::Point2D> a{{0,0}},b{{3,4}};
 bool records_rejected=false,vertices_rejected=false,invalid_rejected=false,overflow_rejected=false;
 try{(void)dm::geometry::gjk_distance_trace(a,b,100,3);}catch(const std::length_error&){records_rejected=true;}
 const auto t=dm::geometry::gjk_distance_trace(a,b,100,4);
 try{(void)dm::geometry::regular_polygon({0,0},1,4,0,3);}catch(const std::length_error&){vertices_rejected=true;}
 const auto p=dm::geometry::regular_polygon({0,0},1,4,0,4);
 try{(void)dm::geometry::gjk_distance_trace({{0,0},{std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN(),0}},b,0,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){invalid_rejected=true;}
 try{(void)dm::geometry::gjk_distance({{1e200,0}},{{0,0}});}catch(const std::overflow_error&){overflow_rejected=true;}
 auto copied=t;copied.events[0].point.x=999;
 const auto zero=dm::geometry::gjk_distance_trace(a,b,0,2);
 std::print("| resource | actual retained amount | rejected limit | rejected |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Complete online records | {} | 3 | {} |\n| Whole generated vertices | {} | 3 | {} |\n",t.events.size(),records_rejected,p.size(),vertices_rejected);
 std::print("\nZero loop visits: distance {:.1f}; stop {}; records {}. Zero optional record quota retains {} records; empty input retains {} record.\n",zero.run.distance,dm::geometry::gjk_stop_name(zero.run.stop),zero.events.size(),dm::geometry::gjk_distance_trace(a,b,100,0).events.size(),dm::geometry::gjk_distance_trace({},b,100,1).events.size());
 std::print("\nIndependent owned history {}; invalid last coordinate before history quota {}; finite intermediate overflow rejected {}; inputs unchanged {}.\n",t.events[0].point.x!=copied.events[0].point.x,invalid_rejected,overflow_rejected,a[0].x==0&&b[0].x==3);
 auto x=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(t.events.size()),3.},{"Retained","Rejected cap"});
 x.title("Online state records").xlab("").ylab("Complete records").y_limits(0,5);
 auto y=dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(p.size()),3.},{"Generated","Rejected cap"});
 y.title("Whole polygon output").xlab("").ylab("Vertices").y_limits(0,5);
 dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(x).add(y).size(1100,490).title("Different resource units have separate admission checks").fit_panels().save_svg("build/gjk_controls.svg");
 if(!records_rejected||!vertices_rejected||!invalid_rejected||!overflow_rejected)throw std::runtime_error("control checks");

}
