> What the checks establish

The hand examples expose actual support choices and retained simplex features.
The original four distances and every sweep value remain reproducible after the
polygon generator moves into the core. Independent development tests explicitly
build exact rational Minkowski hulls and enumerate all boundary projections,
rather than using GJK again. They check ordinary-scale point, segment, unordered,
duplicate and polygon inputs; separate scale witnesses retain the finite failures
instead of treating a broad absolute tolerance as proof of correct contact.
No external dataset is needed for this geometry kernel: controlled coordinates
give analytical answers, known overlap and deliberate changes of units.

Use the returned stopping reason with the stated numerical contract. The support
scan identity explains the measured work, while the fixed loop cap and absolute
tolerances limit the geometric conclusions. In particular, the empty convention,
near-origin zero and floating triangle branch are distinct reasons for a zero
result; none is promoted here to a universal exact collision certificate.
